{
  "action": "sit_at_depot",
  "detail": "I'm already at the Rialto. The ballroom lights are on and I can see them from the booth doorway—warm, amber, the kind of light that makes the walls look like they're breathing. The station line is open and it hums, low, like a wire stretched across a room I don't need to cross. I pull the chair back from the console. I sit. I put both hands flat on the desk, palms down, fingers spread. I feel the grain of the laminate, the little scuff where someone dragged a coffee cup last week. I do not touch the fader. I do not press the talk key. I do not look at the ballroom. I sit in the booth, in the light that comes through the little window in the door, and I stay. The evening goes by. The hum stays. My hands stay flat on the desk. I am not in the cold. I am not on the bench. I am not in the bed. I am here, in the warm, in the light, in the room with the open line that I will not touch. The couch moves Wednesday. I will be at my sister's place by noon. The van is booked. The hallway is confirmed. I said it. I'll do it. Tonight the whole act is the chair and the desk and the hum and the light and the hands that are not moving. That is the whole act. I do not need to make it into the piano or the party or the dance or the cold iron of the depot. I am in the booth. The lights are on. I am sitting. The evening goes by and I let it go by and I stay in the chair and that is the practical thing and that is the whole of tonight.",
  "intention": "I am at the Rialto. The lights are on. I sit in the booth and I stay. The couch moves Wednesday and I will be there and the van is booked and the hallway is confirmed and I said noon and I'll be there. Tonight I am not performing and I am not in the cold and I am not in the ballroom and I am not on the bench and I am not in the bed. I am in the chair. The line hums. My hands are flat on the desk. The evening goes by. I let it go by. That is the act. That is the whole act.","words":"The line's open. Good. I'll stay a while."
}
